<title>UK: Nationwide, Halifax bid for UK defense sale - paper.</title>
<headline>Nationwide, Halifax bid for UK defense sale - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Sunday Telegraph said Britain's two largest building societies, Nationwide and the Halifax, had joined in the battle to privatise homes owned by the Minstry of Defence.</p>
<p>The decision by the two British home-loan banks to enter the fray would pitch them against a consortium led by Nomura, the Japanese investment bank, the report added.</p>
<p>The two building socities were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>In May this year the Ministry of Defence said it had contacted a shortlist of bidders for the planned sale of its married quarters.</p>
<p>The property consists of 58,000 houses in Britain and has a total value which has been estimated at between 1.5 billion and 1.8 billion stg.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
